    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "An invoice's status now counts its credit notes as well as its payments, and `bin/e2e` passes. In the test case (a 100 invoice with a 40 payment and a 60 credit), the project's invoice list shows `$0.00` due and `PAID`.\n\nThe request mentions an OfficeFloor server, but this app is Spring Boot (only the package is named `net.officefloor`). I followed the Spring conventions in `CLAUDE.md`.\n\n**What changed on the server**\n- **New rule** (`Invoice.statusFor(paid, credited)`): drafts and void invoices keep their status. Otherwise an invoice is `PAID` once payments plus credits cover the amount, `PARTIAL` once anything has been paid or credited, and `SENT` if nothing has. An invoice marked paid by hand with nothing recorded against it stays `PAID`, matching the earlier V17 migration.\n- **Shown on read:** the project invoice list, the client statement and the invoice detail page all work the status out with this rule when they load.\n- **Stored value kept in step:**\n  - Recording a payment now stores the status using payments plus credits.\n  - Issuing a credit note now updates the stored status too. Before, it didn't, so a credit that cleared the balance left the invoice owing.\n- **Migration `V55__invoice_status_from_credits.sql`:** re-sets the stored status of existing sent or part-paid invoices that have credit notes.\n\n**Front end:** no changes were needed. It shows the status the server returns, and no `data-testid` was added, renamed or removed.\n\n**One gap:** the all-invoices list and its status filter still read the stored status. That stays correct for anything entered through the app or the migration. But test data seeded straight into the database (like this spec's) isn't recalculated, so such an invoice would show `SENT` there while showing `PAID` on the project page.",
